  "id": "COMPOUND:42545 - PROTEIN:5826",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but interconnected relationship between the compound (4As,10As)-1,1,4A-Trimethyl-7-Propan-2-Yl-2,3,4,9,10,10A-Hexahydrophenanthrene and the cancer cell line SMMC-7721. The compound is identified as a target of multiple entities, including CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which in turn is targeted by (1S,3E,4S,5S,6S)-4,5-dihydroxy-3-(3-methylbut-2-enylidene)-7-oxabicyclo[4.1.0]heptan-2-one and Mycalamide D. All these intermediates ultimately target SMMC-7721, indicating a potential pathway through sialyltransferase activity. The evidence suggests that the compound may act through a sialyltransferase-dependent mechanism, possibly influencing cell proliferation or survival in SMMC-7721 cells. The integration of these pathways highlights the compound's potential role in modulating cellular processes linked to SMMC-7721, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
